@MdBreathe Yeah, no—6mg is going to be hella unpleasant if you're sensitive to nicotine.

I use the smoking cessation tablets from Costco (nicotine kills "food noise" so I don't  feel compelled to snack). They come in 2mg and 4mg doses, 10 tubes of 27 tablets each for ~$60, which lasts me a few months because I only need about 16-24mg/day to not feel snacky.

If it's a turbo boost of energy you want first thing in the morning, take caffeine in capsule form along with twice as much l-Theanine, which will keep the jitters away. So 200mg caffeine and 400mg l-Theanine should help you achieve liftoff. I don't do this every day, but even on days when I'm still just drinking coffee the l-Theanine helps.

